IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art32-36-appeals`
IMPORT `ind-c-tests-fixtures-g8`

-- ind-c-tests-art32-36: independent tests (author ind-c) of Part 8, Articles 32 to 36.  Row ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c fixtures for Articles 32 to 36`

GIVEN applicant IS A BOOLEAN
      charity IS A BOOLEAN
      ag IS A BOOLEAN
      served IS A BOOLEAN
      nameInterest IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`ind-c appellant` applicant charity ag served nameInterest MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH
        `an applicant for registration` IS applicant
        `a registered charity` IS charity
        `the Attorney General` IS ag
        `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS served
        `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS nameInterest

`ind-c the applicant` MEANS `ind-c appellant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind-c the charity` MEANS `ind-c appellant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind-c the AG` MEANS `ind-c appellant` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`ind-c a person served` MEANS `ind-c appellant` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`ind-c a rival with an interest in the name` MEANS `ind-c appellant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`ind-c a member of the public` MEANS `ind-c appellant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind-c a registered rival with an interest in the name` MEANS `ind-c appellant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

GIVEN who IS AN `Appellant under Article 33`
      subject IS A `Subject of a decision of the Commissioner`
      outcome IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
      own IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appeal under Article 33`
`ind-c appeal` who subject outcome own MEANS
    `Appeal under Article 33` WITH
        appellant IS who
        `decision appealed` IS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS subject, outcome IS outcome
        `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS own

GIVETH AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
`ind-c does` MEANS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
`ind-c refuses` MEANS `the Commissioner refuses`

-- The right of appeal with the third-party facts of 33(5) set so that no ground holds (they are read only for 33(5)).
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33`
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`ind-c right` interp appeal MEANS
    `Art 33 the right of appeal` interp appeal TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- The right of a third party, given whether the test was met at each time and whether the name was undesirable at each time.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
      who IS AN `Appellant under Article 33`
      testAtApplication IS A BOOLEAN
      testAtAppeal IS A BOOLEAN
      nameBadAtApplication IS A BOOLEAN
      nameBadAtAppeal IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`ind-c third-party right` interp who testAtApplication testAtAppeal nameBadAtApplication nameBadAtAppeal MEANS
    `Art 33 the right of appeal` interp (`ind-c appeal` who `whether to register an applicant, Article 11` `ind-c does` FALSE) testAtApplication testAtAppeal nameBadAtApplication nameBadAtAppeal

GIVEN standard IS A `Standard that a decision is said to fall short of`
      respect IS A `Respect in which a decision is said to fall short`
GIVETH A `Ground alleged in an appeal`
`ind-c ground` standard respect MEANS `Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS standard, `respect alleged` IS respect

§ `ind-c Article 33 -- who may appeal what`

-- A33-01 .. A33-03: an applicant
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the applicant` `whether to register an applicant, Article 11` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the applicant` `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the applicant` `whether to register an applicant, Article 11` `ind-c does` TRUE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A33-04, A33-05: deregistration under Article 16
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16` `ind-c does` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
-- A33-06 (pre-committed ambiguous; reading A taken): a deregistration granted on the charity's own application
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)` `ind-c does` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 with F8.16 B` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)` `ind-c does` TRUE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A33-07: a refusal to deregister under 15(3)(b) is not appealable by the charity; the AG may appeal it
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the AG` `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)` `ind-c refuses` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
-- F8.4 B (an unlisted decision appealable by analogy), by that reading's definition
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 with F8.4 B` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(2)(a)`
-- A33-08 .. A33-11
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(b)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)` `ind-c does` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(c)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(d)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(e)`
-- A33-12: a refusal of permission to amend a payments statement (13(11)(b)) is unlisted
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `any other matter` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A33-13: a general-section charity refused entry in the restricted section
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the charity` `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)` `ind-c refuses` TRUE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A33-14 .. A33-17: notices
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c a person served` `whether to impose a requirement contained in a notice under Article 26` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c a person served` `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` (`ind-c appellant` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c a member of the public` `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A33-18: the AG, any decision
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the AG` `whether to register an applicant, Article 11` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c the AG` `any other matter` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
-- A33-19 .. A33-24, A33-26: a third party against a registration
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a rival with an interest in the name` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a rival with an interest in the name` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a rival with an interest in the name` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a member of the public` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a member of the public` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a member of the public` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `Art 33 the right of appeal` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c a member of the public` `whether to register an applicant, Article 11` `ind-c refuses` FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A33-25 (pre-committed ambiguous; reading A taken): a registered charity with an interest in the name is excluded; on reading B it is not
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a registered rival with an interest in the name` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 with F8.13 B` `ind-c a registered rival with an interest in the name` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
-- F8.18 B (a different ground at each time), by that reading's definition
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c a rival with an interest in the name` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `ind-c third-party right` `ind-c G8 with F8.18 B` `ind-c a rival with an interest in the name` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5) on grounds that differ between the two times`
-- A33-27: a governor of a deregistered charity, in the governor's own name
#ASSERT `ind-c right` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c a member of the public` `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16` `ind-c does` FALSE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 33 the person may appeal the decision` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c appeal` `ind-c a member of the public` `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16` `ind-c does` FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `ind-c Articles 34 and 35 -- grounds and powers`

-- A34-01: the grounds of 34(1)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`ind-c ground` `wrong` `the facts`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`ind-c ground` `unreasonable` `the law`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`ind-c ground` `wrong` `its merits`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`ind-c ground` `neither wrong nor unreasonable` `the facts`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`ind-c ground` `wrong` `some other respect`)
-- A34-03: the tribunal remits, substitutes or dismisses
#ASSERT `Art 34(3)(a) the way is one the tribunal may use` `remit the decision to the Commissioner`
#ASSERT `Art 34(3)(a) the way is one the tribunal may use` `substitute the decision of the tribunal or court for that of the Commissioner`
#ASSERT `Art 34(3)(a) the way is one the tribunal may use` `dismiss the appeal`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(3)(a) the way is one the tribunal may use` `remit the decision to the tribunal`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(3)(a) the way is one the tribunal may use` `substitute the decision of the court for that of the tribunal`
-- A35-01 .. A35-05
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `ind-c G8 A` TRUE FALSE (`ind-c ground` `unreasonable` `all the circumstances of the case`)
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `ind-c G8 A` FALSE TRUE (`ind-c ground` `unreasonable` `all the circumstances of the case`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `ind-c G8 A` FALSE FALSE (`ind-c ground` `unreasonable` `all the circumstances of the case`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `ind-c G8 A` TRUE FALSE (`ind-c ground` `wrong` `the facts`)
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `ind-c G8 with F8.5 B` TRUE FALSE (`ind-c ground` `wrong` `the facts`)
-- A35-06: the court's five ways
#ASSERT `Art 35(2) the way is one the court may use` `remit the decision to the tribunal`
#ASSERT `Art 35(2) the way is one the court may use` `remit the decision to the Commissioner`
#ASSERT `Art 35(2) the way is one the court may use` `substitute the decision of the court for that of the tribunal`
#ASSERT `Art 35(2) the way is one the court may use` `substitute the decision of the tribunal or court for that of the Commissioner`
#ASSERT `Art 35(2) the way is one the court may use` `dismiss the appeal`

§ `ind-c Article 36 -- time limits and substituted decisions`

`ind-c appeal dates` MEANS `Dates of an appeal under Article 36(2)` WITH `day of the decision` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `day of the notice of the decision` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 3), `day the appeal was lodged` IS YMD 2027 9 1

-- A36-02: the Law prescribes no time limit; without the Order there is no answer, and with no limit prescribed the appeal is in time
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 36(2) the appeal is in time` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c appeal dates` NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the appeal is in time` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c appeal dates` (JUST `no Order has prescribed a time limit`)
-- A36-03: a substituted decision may take effect from a date before the order
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) the date from which the substituted decision takes effect` (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) the substituted decision takes effect from a date before the date of the order` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 36(3) the substituted decision takes effect from a date before the date of the order` (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 6 1)

-- 36(4), with the order dated 1 June 2026; the act is an offence only by the order's operation.
GIVEN effective IS A DATE
      act IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c offence by the order alone` effective act MEANS
    `Art 36(4) the act is an offence in the light of the order` (`Art 36(3) the substituted decision takes effect from a date before the date of the order` effective (YMD 2026 6 1)) (act LESS THAN YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE TRUE

-- A36-04 .. A36-08
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c offence by the order alone` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT `ind-c offence by the order alone` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 2)
#ASSERT `ind-c offence by the order alone` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `ind-c offence by the order alone` (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c offence by the order alone` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2024 6 1)
-- an act that is an offence apart from the order stays one
#ASSERT `Art 36(4) the act is an offence in the light of the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
